From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anakin Childerhose <anakin@childerhose.ca>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:34:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ast: make Diagnostics::foreach public

A language server needs to read each diagnostic's message, hints and
location to report them to the editor. foreach was the only way to
iterate the diagnostics, but it was private, leaving only emit()'s
formatted text.
---
 src/ast/diagnostic.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ast/diagnostic.h b/src/ast/diagnostic.h
index e4ca195..4752d21 100644
--- a/src/ast/diagnostic.h
+++ b/src/ast/diagnostic.h
@@ -134,7 +134,8 @@ public:
   // adds all diagnostics from some other set.
   void add(Diagnostics&& other);
 
-private:
+  // Calls `fn` with each diagnostic of the given severity, in the order they
+  // were added.
   void foreach(Severity severity,
                std::function<void(const Diagnostic&)> fn) const
   {
@@ -147,6 +148,7 @@ private:
     }
   }
 
+private:
   // Two-dimensional vector with all diagnostics. The first level is indexed by
   // severity, and the second level is the set of diagnostics for that level.
   //
